## Part 1: Core Data Modules

### Module 1: Property Management

#### 1.1 Property DocType
Represents the hospitality asset (homestay, villa, hostel, hotel).

**Fields:**
- `name` (doctype id): e.g., "PROP-0001"
- `property_name` (string, required): "Pondicherry Homestay A"
- `property_type` (select): Homestay / Villa / Hotel / Hostel / Resort / Guesthouse
- `location_description` (text): Address, landmarks, directions
- `latitude`, `longitude` (float): Map pinning
- `total_rooms` (integer): Computed from Room count
- `total_units` (integer): For serviced apartments
- `check_in_time` (time): Default 2:00 PM
- `check_out_time` (time): Default 11:00 AM
- `amenities` (text): WiFi, AC, Pool, Parking, etc.
- `house_rules` (text): Pet policy, noise restrictions, etc.
- `contact_person` (link to User)
- `email`, `phone` (contact)
- `status` (select): Active / Inactive / Maintenance
- `description` (markdown): Rich text, for listing
- `banner_image` (image): Main property photo
- `images` (table): Gallery of photos

**Permissions:**
- Owner (property contact_person) can edit all fields
- Staff can view except financial fields
- API read-only for marketplace

